Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0017.
VLLM_MOE_GATE_FIRST=1 (default off): the MoE runner applies the router gate before it forks the shared experts onto the
aux stream, instead of after. The router feeds top-k and the routed experts, the critical path of a decode MoE; the
shared expert only has to finish before the final add. Forked first, the shared expert's kernels take the SMs and the
router GEMM waits for them: on V4.1 decode (2x GB10, TP=2, k=5) the router starts a median 19.3 us after its input is
ready, over 1,400 profiled layers (LOG Oct 11 05:52). Same math, same order of floating-point work on each stream.

